        "title": "docs: repair ClawHub docs navigation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a docs navigation problem where the ClawHub tab pointed to several pages that are not present in the repository, and legacy ClawHub redirects pointed at `/clawhub` even though no ClawHub landing page existed.\n\nAI-assisted.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a small ClawHub landing page that links to the existing CLI and publishing docs, trims the ClawHub nav to routes that exist, adds the required zh-CN glossary labels for the new ClawHub links, and regenerates the docs map so route metadata stays current. The landing page describes ClawHub as surfacing release trust details instead of promising that all community releases are trusted.\n\n## User Impact\n\nReaders can open the ClawHub docs hub and navigate to the available ClawHub docs without hitting missing docs routes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git rebase origin/main` - passed; rebased branch onto `7ae5996bb3c5c8d072b13288e974f7c52a719fe2`.\n- `git diff --check -- docs/clawhub/index.md docs/docs.json docs/docs_map.md docs/.i18n/glossary.zh-CN.json` - passed.\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 docs/clawhub/index.md` - passed.\n- `pnpm docs:check-mdx` - passed: 708 files checked.\n- `pnpm docs:check-links` - passed: 5,826 internal links checked, 0 broken links.\n- `pnpm docs:map:check` - passed: docs map is up to date.\n- `pnpm docs:check-i18n-glossary` - passed.",
